// ============================================================================
// COLLISION BOX SWITCHER ENTITY
// ============================================================================
// 
// This entity contains component groups and events for all unique mob collision box
// dimensions extracted from vanilla Minecraft Bedrock mob entities, plus gap-filled widths.
//
// IMPORTANT NOTES:
// 
// 1. WHY 384 COMPONENT GROUPS/EVENTS INSTEAD OF 84?
//    - Analysis found 84+ unique mob entities with collision boxes
//    - Collision boxes are extracted from BOTH main components AND component_groups
//    - This includes baby, adult, and other variant collision boxes (e.g., turtle baby/adult, zombie variants)
//    - However, many mobs share the same collision box dimensions
//    - Originally 39 unique widths were extracted from entities
//    - Since height is fixed at 0.05, we only need unique widths
//    - Gaps were filled between 0.2 and 4.0 to create 384 total widths
//    - Example: Multiple mobs with different heights but same width (0.50) all use
//      the same collision box: 0.50 x 0.05 (width varies, height fixed at 0.05)
//
// 2. NO ENTITY_SPAWNED EVENT:
//    - This entity does NOT have a minecraft:entity_spawned event
//    - You must manually trigger the appropriate collision box event based on your needs
//    - Use events like "0.50_0.05_set" to switch to that collision box size
//    - Each event adds its corresponding component group and removes all others
//
// 3. COLLISION BOX REDUCTION AND FIXED HEIGHT:
//    - ALL collision box widths have been reduced by 0.0 from their original values
//    - This 0.0 deduction was applied to width during extraction
//    - ALL collision box heights are FIXED at 0.05 (regardless of original height)
//    - Example: Original 0.60 x 1.80 becomes 0.60 x 0.05 (width reduced by 0.0, height fixed at 0.05)
//    - The reduction and height fix were applied during generation
//    - Note: ALL collision boxes from component_groups are included (baby, adult, and other variants)
//      This means entities like turtle contribute both baby (0.6x0.2) and adult (1.2x0.4) collision boxes
//
// 4. GAP FILLING:
//    - After extracting 39 unique widths from entities, gaps were filled between 0.2 and 4.0
//    - Missing widths are generated in increments of 0.01 (e.g., 0.20, 0.21, 0.22, ..., 4.00)
//    - This ensures a complete range of 384 collision box widths is available
//    - Gap-filled widths use the same fixed height of 0.05
//    - To adjust the gap filling range, modify MIN_WIDTH and MAX_WIDTH in generate_collision_box_entity.py
//
// 5. COMPRESSION (if enabled):
//    - Component group names are shortened: "a0", "a1", "a2", ... instead of "0.20_0.05_collision_box"
//    - Event names are shortened: "e0", "e1", "e2", ... instead of "0.20_0.05_set"
//    - JSON is minified (no whitespace) to reduce file size
//    - This is lossless compression - functionality is identical, just smaller file size
//    - To disable compression, set USE_SHORT_NAMES = False in generate_collision_box_entity.py
//
// USAGE:
//    Trigger events like: "<width>_0.05_set" to switch collision boxes (or "e0", "e1", etc. if compressed)
//    Example: "0.50_0.05_set" sets collision box to width=0.50, height=0.05
//    Note: All events use 0.05 for height since height is fixed at 0.05
//
// ============================================================================
